{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When any man has a discharge from his body, his discharge is impure.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: 'his discharge is impure' teaches that even a single drop defiles. Zov resembles the water of barley dough and resembles the white of a spoiled egg. Seminal emission is bound like the white of an unsppoiled egg. And it says: <b>the flow of his body, his discharge</b>, to say that his discharge is like mucous (ריר) that issues clear. Or 'it seals his body' — that which issues thick and blocks the opening of the canal, and his body is sealed on account of his discharge. And the reason for the impurity of the zov in a man is because it is a disease of the liver among the communicable diseases, and Scripture required a sacrifice of two turtledoves or two young pigeons, one for a sin-offering and one for a burnt-offering. It required a sin-offering to atone for his sin, that it not cause him illness again; and a burnt-offering sacrifice in order to give thanksgiving to the Holy One, blessed be He, that He healed him and purified him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:27.984468403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}